{%- comment -%}
The WCAG 2.2 conformance levels at which rows list success criteria, in
the order A, AA, AAA, as a phrase: "Level AA", "Levels A and AA", or
"Levels A, AA and AAA". A level no row lists is left out, so the report
never claims a level its table does not hold.
{%- endcomment -%}
{%- assign a = false -%}
{%- assign aa = false -%}
{%- assign aaa = false -%}
{%- for row in rows -%}
{%- capture level %}{% render "criteria/wcag-level.liquid", id: row.criterion %}{% endcapture -%}
{%- case level -%}
{%- when "A" -%}{%- assign a = true -%}
{%- when "AA" -%}{%- assign aa = true -%}
{%- when "AAA" -%}{%- assign aaa = true -%}
{%- endcase -%}
{%- endfor -%}
{%- capture levels %}{% if a %} A{% endif %}{% if aa %} AA{% endif %}{% if aaa %} AAA{% endif %}{% endcapture -%}
{%- assign levels = levels | strip | split: " " -%}
{%- if levels.size > 1 %}Levels {% else %}Level {% endif -%}
{%- render "list.liquid", items: levels -%}
